o overall scores, results are reported by race/ethnicity, gender, type of school, and other demographic groups. The report also provides information about student performance on sample questions as well as data related to teaching and learning during and after the pandemic.\n\n## Online Availability\n\n- [Browse the full results in the 2022 NAEP Mathematics Report Card.](https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/?grade=4)\n- [Browse the 2022 NAEP Mathematics Highlights.](https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/)\n\n## You may also like\n\n Workshop/Training\n\n### Data Science for Education (DS4EDU)\n\n July 01, 2026\n\n Publication/Product Release\n\n### Mathematics Intervention Toolkit: High-Quality Res...\n\n April 29, 2026\n\n Research insights\n\n### Partners in Progress: Examining Students’ Pathways...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"991d16a20d485eb2\">>>"}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775744031550}}
