{"type": "message", "id": "02c9633b", "parentId": "9955568b", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T14:14:21.525Z", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "I found some useful information:\n\n1. **South Carolina**: According to ed.sc.gov - \"South Carolina eighth-graders' average score was 269\" - This is BELOW 270, so it does NOT meet the NAEP criteria.\n\n2. The CSG South document mentions:\n- \"Virginia (279) was the only state to score above the national average\"\n- \"Missouri (272), North Carolina (274), Tennessee (272), and Texas (273)\"\n- National average was 274 for 8th grade math in 2022\n\nI still need specific scores for Kansas, Kentucky, and Arizona. Let me search for those specific scores and also for the FRED housing data.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning"}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_urudgR6bE2c4Z0WJBwCNR8GR", "name": "web_search", "arguments": {"query": "Kansas NAEP 2022 grade 8 math score 274"}}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_PUnFl1q1DElzAbvHLPjK3Ddd", "name": "web_search", "arguments": {"query": "Kentucky NAEP 2022 grade 8 math score"}}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_l7tYyFLRMAOzm5CvlGawWOpJ", "name": "web_search", "arguments": {"query": "Arizona NAEP 2022 grade 8 math score"}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "openrouter", "model": "z-ai/glm-5", "usage": {"input": 9104, "output": 365, "cacheRead": 16384, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 25853, "cost": {"input": 0.0054624, "output": 0.0006934999999999999, "cacheRead": 0.001949696, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.008105596}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1775744057237, "responseId": "gen-1775744057-XXyGTqaEnYio7ixNkIHu"}}
{"type": "message", "id": "6bbf3823", "parentId": "02c9633b", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T14:14:22.479Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_urudgR6bE2c4Z0WJBwCNR8GR", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"Kansas NAEP 2022 grade 8 math score 274\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 952,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0a781ddc2ee316c0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT KANSAS  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0a781ddc2ee316c0\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011KS8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"09109ebf08a5b865\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOTE: The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"09109ebf08a5b865\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"80a6c59e1976810b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"80a6c59e1976810b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"eefff92633cd7d8d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTo compare average mathematics scores between states/jurisdictions and the nation (public), use the NAEP State Profiles Tool. ... In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, the size of the score differences ranged from 2 to 14 points.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"eefff92633cd7d8d\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"28663cc96a45607b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n72% of Kansas 8th Graders Aren’t Proficient in Math | Aligned\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"28663cc96a45607b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.wearealigned.org/blogs/72-kansas-8th-graders-arent-proficient-math\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5b36f7830766c0ae\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAccording to the 2022 NAEP (Nation’s Report Card): 72% of Kansas 8th graders are below proficient in math. Kansas’s average 8th-grade score: 274, which is <strong>slightly above the national average, but far from top-performing states</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5b36f7830766c0ae\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"August 1, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.wearealigned.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b342b737cb0b8d12\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 National Assessment of Educational Progress Grade 8 Mathematics Results\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b342b737cb0b8d12\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.fldoe.org/core/fileparse.php/7667/urlt/2022NAEPGrade8Math.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ddf23235f878b1d9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOTE: <strong>The NAEP Mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ddf23235f878b1d9\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.fldoe.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"58697398a3431feb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: Mathematics Highlights 2022\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"58697398a3431feb\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9ef28d45b1300e4d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLooking at state/jurisdiction performance for eighth-graders in public schools, average scores were lower in 51 states/jurisdictions and not significantly different in 2. This is the largest number of states/jurisdictions with score declines in grade 8 mathematics going back to 2003. Among the states/jurisdictions with score declines, 18 scored lower than the national average score for public school students in 2022; 16 had average scores that were not significantly different from the national public average; and 17 scored higher. Explore detailed state average score results in the NAEP Mathematics Report Card\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9ef28d45b1300e4d\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "Kansas NAEP 2022 grade 8 math score 274", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 952, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0a781ddc2ee316c0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT KANSAS  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0a781ddc2ee316c0\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011KS8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"09109ebf08a5b865\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNOTE: The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"09109ebf08a5b865\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"80a6c59e1976810b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"80a6c59e1976810b\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"eefff92633cd7d8d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTo compare average mathematics scores between states/jurisdictions and the nation (public), use the NAEP State Profiles Tool. ... In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, the size of the score differences ranged from 2 to 14 points.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"eefff92633cd7d8d\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"28663cc96a45607b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n72% of Kansas 8th Graders Aren’t Proficient in Math | Aligned\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"28663cc96a45607b\">>>", "url": "https://www.wearealigned.org/blogs/72-kansas-8th-graders-arent-proficient-math", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5b36f7830766c0ae\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAccording to the 2022 NAEP (Nation’s Report Card): 72% of Kansas 8th graders are below proficient in math. Kansas’s average 8th-grade score: 274, which is <strong>slightly above the national average, but far from top-performing states</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5b36f7830766c0ae\">>>", "published": "August 1, 2025", "siteName": "www.wearealigned.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b342b737cb0b8d12\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 National Assessment of Educational Progress Grade 8 Mathematics Results\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b342b737cb0b8d12\">>>", "url": "https://www.fldoe.org/core/fileparse.php/7667/urlt/2022NAEPGrade8Math.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ddf23235f878b1d9\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNOTE: <strong>The NAEP Mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ddf23235f878b1d9\">>>", "siteName": "www.fldoe.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"58697398a3431feb\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: Mathematics Highlights 2022\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"58697398a3431feb\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9ef28d45b1300e4d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nLooking at state/jurisdiction performance for eighth-graders in public schools, average scores were lower in 51 states/jurisdictions and not significantly different in 2. This is the largest number of states/jurisdictions with score declines in grade 8 mathematics going back to 2003. Among the states/jurisdictions with score declines, 18 scored lower than the national average score for public school students in 2022; 16 had average scores that were not significantly different from the national public average; and 17 scored higher. Explore detailed state average score results in the NAEP Mathematics Report Card\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9ef28d45b1300e4d\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775744062479}}
