{"type": "message", "id": "b982644d", "parentId": "2d47e329", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T14:14:22.571Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_l7tYyFLRMAOzm5CvlGawWOpJ", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"Arizona NAEP 2022 grade 8 math score\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 1040,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d9d050033ab9fc2b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT ARIZONA  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d9d050033ab9fc2b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011AZ8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dcc67a87704de79b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOTE: Puerto Rico was not included in the comparison results. AVERAGE SCORES FOR STATE/JURISDICTION AND THE NATION (PUBLIC) ... White students. This performance gap was not significantly different from that in 2000 ... NOTE: The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from <strong>0 to 500</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dcc67a87704de79b\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"faceab93b34007fa\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"faceab93b34007fa\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"31d8f50306bfb552\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTo compare average mathematics scores between states/jurisdictions and the nation (public), use the NAEP State Profiles Tool. ... In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, the size of the score differences ranged from 2 to 14 points. The average score decline for public schools in the nation decreased by 5 points. To view score changes for fourth-grade ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"31d8f50306bfb552\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7d455a9d0b7d1b82\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 National Assessment of Educational Progress Grade 8 Mathematics Results\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7d455a9d0b7d1b82\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.fldoe.org/core/fileparse.php/7667/urlt/2022NAEPGrade8Math.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2fe72d2daf117e7e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Grade 8 Mathematics · State Score Change Summary · Average Scale Scores: 2019-2022 · US map. Data are provided in the table below. Between 2019 and 2022 · 0 · states/jurisdictions · had a score increase · 2 · states/jurisdictions · had no significant change in score · 51 · states/jurisdictions · had a score decrease · + National · Public · DoDEA · Alabama · Kentucky · North Dakota · Utah · Alaska · Arizona ·\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2fe72d2daf117e7e\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.fldoe.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7c14862806e67fab\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe New NAEP Scores Highlight a Standards Gap in Many States - FutureEd\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7c14862806e67fab\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.future-ed.org/the-new-naep-scores-highlight-a-standards-gap-in-many-states/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5f0f6fc5681074b3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nForty-seven states improved NAEP math proficiency rates between 2022 and 2024 in fourth grade and 36 states did so in eighth grade. But proficiency rates remain below 2019 levels in 34 states in fourth-grade and in all but one state in eighth-grade. Similarly, math proficiency rates rose on nearly every state’s standardized tests during the same period. While state math scores declined dramatically between 2019 and 2022, particularly in eighth grade, only in Arizona, Arkansas, Florida, Idaho, and Vermont in fourth grade and Arkansas, Michigan, and Missouri in eighth grade did state test scores decline between 2022 and 2024.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5f0f6fc5681074b3\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 10, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.future-ed.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1515d7a74a70e468\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP | Arizona Department of Education\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1515d7a74a70e468\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.azed.gov/assessment/naep\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"013e9a625eb9b5f0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nnaep-logo.jpg The National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP) is the largest nationally continuing evaluation of the condition of education in the United States. NAEP has served as a national yardstick of student achievement since 1969.Through The Nation’s Report Card, NAEP informs the public what American students know in various subject areas and compares achievement among states, large urban districts, and various student groups.NAEP is a congressionally mandated program administered by the National Center for Education Statistics (NCES) within the U.S.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"013e9a625eb9b5f0\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"July 14, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.azed.gov\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "Arizona NAEP 2022 grade 8 math score", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 1040, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_s